{"type":"ui_investigation_summary","content":{"id":"root","type":"container","props":{"layout":"vertical"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"summary","type":"card","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"summary__hdr","type":"card-header","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"summary__row","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"summary__title","type":"card-title","props":{},"text":"GPU training throughput drop — FSx for Lustre, EFA/NCCL, or GPU?","children":[]},{"id":"summary__status","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"info"},"text":"investigating","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"summary__body","type":"card-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"summary__incident_title","type":"title","props":{"level":3},"text":"Incident","children":[]},{"id":"summary__incident","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"GPU training cluster performance investigation: training throughput has degraded and the cause is unconfirmed — could be storage (FSx for Lustre filesystem fs-077c776983688ad76, SCRATCH_2, 1200 GiB SSD, us-west-2, account 111122223333), network (EFA/NCCL), or GPUs. No specific start time was given, so the impact window defaults to the last 72 hours: ~2026-09-28T04:08Z to 2026-10-01T04:08Z.","children":[]},{"id":"summary__cause_title","type":"title","props":{"level":3},"text":"Cause","children":[]},{"id":"summary__cause","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"FSx for Lustre has been ruled out as the bottleneck (peak utilization just 1-6% over 72h). Leading observation: the GPU compute fleet for the training cluster distributed-training-triage-b200 is currently scaled to zero / not running — this coincides with the near-zero FSx read activity, but the root cause of the throughput drop is not yet confirmed, and recovering GPU worker history is blocked by the CloudTrail restriction.","children":[]},{"id":"summary__focus_title","type":"title","props":{"level":3},"text":"Current focus","children":[]},{"id":"summary__focus","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"Determining how to recover GPU worker identity/metrics for the impact window despite the CloudTrail gap — no GPU compute nodes are currently running to inspect directly.","children":[]},{"id":"summary__plan_title","type":"title","props":{"level":3},"text":"Plan","children":[]},{"id":"summary__plan","type":"list","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"summary__plan_0","type":"list-item","props":{},"text":"Find an alternate path to historical GPU worker instance IDs (e.g. Slurm job/scheduler logs) since CloudTrail is blocked","children":[]},{"id":"summary__plan_1","type":"list-item","props":{},"text":"If instance IDs are recovered, query GPU utilization and EFA/NCCL metrics over the impact window","children":[]},{"id":"summary__plan_2","type":"list-item","props":{},"text":"Review Slurm/ParallelCluster scaling behavior to determine if scale-to-zero was expected or a failure","children":[]},{"id":"summary__plan_3","type":"list-item","props":{},"text":"Determine if the capacity-block reservation history offers further clues on job scheduling","children":[]}]}]}]},{"id":"records","type":"card","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__hdr","type":"card-header","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__title","type":"card-title","props":{},"text":"Findings & evidence","children":[]}]},{"id":"records__body","type":"card-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__acc","type":"accordion","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput","type":"accordion-item","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__trg","type":"accordion-trigger","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__row","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__badge","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"secondary"},"text":"hypothesis","children":[]},{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__summary","type":"text","props":{},"text":"SCRATCH_2 FSx at minimum size may be throughput-limited — ruled out","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__body","type":"accordion-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__desc","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"SCRATCH_2 FSx at minimum size (1200 GiB) has a theoretical throughput ceiling of ~240 MB/s, which was considered a plausible bottleneck for a B200 training job. Ruled out: over the 72h window, NetworkThroughputUtilization (OSS0000) peaked at only 1.02% and FileServerDiskThroughputUtilization peaked at 5.66% — nowhere near saturation.","children":[]},{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__obs","type":"list","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_hyp-fsx-scratch2-throughput__obs_0","type":"list-item","props":{},"text":"obs-fsx-utilization-low","children":[]}]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop","type":"accordion-item","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop__trg","type":"accordion-trigger","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop__row","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop__badge","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"info"},"text":"symptom","children":[]},{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop__summary","type":"text","props":{},"text":"B200 training throughput drop — 2026-09-28T04:08:00Z → 2026-10-01T04:08:00Z","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop__body","type":"accordion-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop__desc","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"Training throughput for the B200 benchmark job has degraded over the last few days. Impact window defaults to the last 72 hours (2026-09-28T04:08Z to 2026-10-01T04:08Z) as no specific start time was given. Root cause not yet isolated among storage (FSx for Lustre), network (EFA/NCCL), or GPU utilization.","children":[]},{"id":"records__rec_symptom-training-throughput-drop__time","type":"text","props":{},"text":"2026-09-28T04:08:00Z → 2026-10-01T04:08:00Z","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_gap-cloudtrail-health-blocked","type":"accordion-item","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_gap-cloudtrail-health-blocked__trg","type":"accordion-trigger","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_gap-cloudtrail-health-blocked__row","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_gap-cloudtrail-health-blocked__badge","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"outline"},"text":"gap","children":[]},{"id":"records__rec_gap-cloudtrail-health-blocked__summary","type":"text","props":{},"text":"CloudTrail blocked — cannot recover historical GPU worker instance IDs","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_gap-cloudtrail-health-blocked__body","type":"accordion-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_gap-cloudtrail-health-blocked__desc","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"CloudTrail lookup_events (RunInstances/TerminateInstances) is not permitted in this environment ('cloudtrail service operations are not allowed'). Since no GPU compute nodes are currently running in the target VPC, this is the only way to recover the instance IDs of the GPU workers that ran during the impact window (2026-09-28T04:08Z–2026-10-01T04:08Z). Without those IDs, the GPU/EFA/NCCL telemetry subagents cannot query CloudWatch for the relevant historical GPU utilization, EFA, or NCCL metrics — this is a hard blocker on the compute and network branches of the investigation. (Note: the AWS Health API required the us-east-1 global endpoint — regional calls failed — but once called correctly it returned zero events in-window; that was a transient tool-use issue, not itself a gap.)","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_obs-fsx-utilization-low","type":"accordion-item","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-fsx-utilization-low__trg","type":"accordion-trigger","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-fsx-utilization-low__row","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-fsx-utilization-low__badge","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"secondary"},"text":"observation","children":[]},{"id":"records__rec_obs-fsx-utilization-low__summary","type":"text","props":{},"text":"FSx utilization metrics show no saturation","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_obs-fsx-utilization-low__body","type":"accordion-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-fsx-utilization-low__desc","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"Over the full 72h window (2026-09-28T04:08Z to 2026-10-01T04:08Z): NetworkThroughputUtilization (OSS0000) peaked at 1.02%, FileServerDiskThroughputUtilization peaked at 5.66%, MDS0000 CPUUtilization peaked at 10.14%. FreeDataStorageCapacity stayed ~97% free (constant). MetadataOperations flat (~4,500-4,525/day). ClientConnections constant at 1 the whole window. DataReadBytes essentially flat at ~6 bytes/sec; DataWriteBytes = 0. None of the saturation metrics approached the ~90% flag threshold at any point. The near-zero read volume is itself notable: the job barely read from this filesystem during the window, and only one Lustre client was ever mounted — this points away from storage and toward the GPU compute fleet or dataloader as the real locus of the problem.","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_obs-no-gpu-nodes-running","type":"accordion-item","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-no-gpu-nodes-running__trg","type":"accordion-trigger","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-no-gpu-nodes-running__row","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-no-gpu-nodes-running__badge","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"secondary"},"text":"observation","children":[]},{"id":"records__rec_obs-no-gpu-nodes-running__summary","type":"text","props":{},"text":"GPU compute fleet in target cluster is scaled to zero","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"records__rec_obs-no-gpu-nodes-running__body","type":"accordion-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"records__rec_obs-no-gpu-nodes-running__desc","type":"markdown","props":{},"text":"Target cluster confirmed as AWS ParallelCluster (Slurm) 3.16.0, cluster `distributed-training-triage-b200`, in VPC vpc-0028c20959269e96f, which mounts the FSx filesystem. HyperPod clusters (`skilltest-hp-slurm`, `skilltest-hp-eks-hp`) are definitively ruled out as unrelated — they live in a different subnet (subnet-05943ef4a877aeb55) and run small g5.xlarge/g5.2xlarge/g5.4xlarge instances, not B200/B300 hardware.

No GPU compute nodes are running in the target VPC or FSx subnet at report time — confirmed empty across instance-type filters (p6*/p5*/p4d*/g6*/g5*) and the FSx subnet directly. Only two t3.medium head nodes exist (one for the b200 cluster, one for an unrelated 'distributed-training-triage' cluster); both are healthy (EC2 status checks ok/ok, no AWS Health events in window 2026-09-28T04:08Z–2026-10-01T04:08Z, checked via the us-east-1 global Health endpoint). The ParallelCluster Slurm GPU compute fleet is scaled to zero / terminated — this may be expected dynamic Slurm scaling rather than a failure, but it means no live GPU/EFA telemetry is currently observable.

One running p6-b300.48xlarge instance (i-0ec31e7eff7635265, 'b300-xid-verify') was found consuming the account's only active capacity-block reservation (cr-0580a9d7420fd589a, active until 2026-10-03T11:30Z), but it is confirmed UNRELATED to this investigation: different VPC (vpc-0968395d1c4c18fbc), untagged, does not mount the target FSx. It must not be treated as a node of this training job.","children":[]}]}]}]}]}]},{"id":"task-list","type":"card","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"task-list__hdr","type":"card-header","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"task-list__title","type":"card-title","props":{},"text":"Agent tasks","children":[]}]},{"id":"task-list__body","type":"card-content","props":{},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"task-list__task_cluster-inventory","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"task-list__task_cluster-inventory__status","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"success"},"text":"completed","children":[]},{"id":"task-list__task_cluster-inventory__text","type":"text","props":{},"text":"Inventory GPU cluster compute/network topology — Confirmed: ParallelCluster Slurm (distributed-training-triage-b200) GPU fleet scaled to zero; HyperPod ruled out; head nodes healthy; CloudTrail blocked","children":[]}]},{"id":"task-list__task_fsx-metrics","type":"container","props":{"layout":"horizontal"},"text":null,"children":[{"id":"task-list__task_fsx-metrics__status","type":"badge","props":{"variant":"success"},"text":"completed","children":[]},{"id":"task-list__task_fsx-metrics__text","type":"text","props":{},"text":"Query FSx for Lustre throughput/IOPS/CPU metrics for saturation — Confirmed FSx not saturated (peak network throughput 1.02%, disk throughput 5.66%)","children":[]}]}]}]}]}}

